IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cr2-pension-adjustments`

-- Tests of cr2-pension-adjustments.l4 (regulations 78.3 and 78.4). Layer 1.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the regulation and the months counted on a
-- calendar, before the rules were run. A month is written by its first day.
--
-- The 65th birthday falls in month M; section 2(2) of the Act deems the contributor to reach 65 at the
-- beginning of the month AFTER M, and that month is "the month in which the contributor reaches 65".

§ `Tests -- regulations 78.3 and 78.4`

§§ `The month in which the contributor reaches 65 (section 2(2) applied)`

-- Born 15 March 1960: 65th birthday 15 March 2025; deemed to reach 65 on 1 April 2025.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 1)
-- Born on the first day of a month: the birthday is still in that month, so the following month.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 4 1)
-- Born in December: the following month is January of the next year.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 and 78.4 — the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 12 31) EQUALS (YMD 2026 1 1)

§§ `78.3 -- which pensions it speaks to`

-- Born 15 March 1960 reaches 65 in April 2025. A pension payable in March 2025 is payable before that month.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 20)
-- Payable in April 2025, the very month the contributor reaches 65: not before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78.3 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 4 1))
-- Payable in May 2025: after, not before.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78.3 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month before the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 5 1))

§§ `78.3 -- A, the number of months, capped at 60`

-- Born 15 March 1960, pension payable January 2024: January 2024 to March 2025 is 15 months.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS 15
-- Pension payable at 60: born 15 March 1960 reaches 60 in April 2020; April 2020 to March 2025 is exactly 60 months.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS 60
-- One month earlier would be 61 months, so the cap of 60 applies.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS 60
-- The month before the month of reaching 65 is one month.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — A, the number of months from the month the pension becomes payable to the month before the contributor reaches 65 years of age, or 60` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS 1

§§ `78.3 -- B, by the month the pension becomes payable (both edges of every band)`

#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2010 12 31) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2010 12 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2011 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0050
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2011 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0050
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2012 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0052
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2012 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0052
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2013 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0054
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2013 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0054
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2014 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0056
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2014 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0056
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2015 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0058
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2015 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0058
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2016 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0060
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — B, the reduction for each month` (YMD 2031 6 15) EQUALS JUST 0.0060

§§ `78.3 -- the adjustment factor, 1 - (A x B)`

-- Born 15 March 1960, payable January 2024: A is 15 and B is 0.0060, so 1 - 0.09 = 0.91.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.91
-- Payable at 60 (April 2020): A is 60 and B is 0.0060, so 1 - 0.36 = 0.64.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS JUST 0.64
-- Born 15 June 1950 reaches 65 in July 2015. Payable January 2011: A is 54, B is 0.0050, so 1 - 0.27 = 0.73.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2011 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.73
-- Payable December 2011: A is 43, B is 0.0050, so 1 - 0.215 = 0.785.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2011 12 1) EQUALS JUST 0.785
-- Payable January 2012: A is 42, B is 0.0052, so 1 - 0.2184 = 0.7816.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2012 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.7816
-- Payable January 2013: A is 30, B is 0.0054, so 1 - 0.162 = 0.838.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2013 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.838
-- Payable January 2014: A is 18, B is 0.0056, so 1 - 0.1008 = 0.8992.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2014 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.8992
-- Payable January 2015: A is 6, B is 0.0058, so 1 - 0.0348 = 0.9652.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2015 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.9652
-- A month before January 2011: the text gives no B, so it is not covered.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1950 6 15) (YMD 2010 12 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Payable in the month of reaching 65, or after: regulation 78.3 does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) (YMD 2025 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `78.4 -- which pensions it speaks to`

-- Born 15 March 1955 reaches 65 in April 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2020 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78.4 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 30))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 78.4 — the retirement pension becomes payable in a month after the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 1))

§§ `78.4 -- A, the number of months, capped at 60`

-- The month after reaching 65 is May 2020; payable May 2020 is one month.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2020 5 1) EQUALS 1
-- Payable January 2023: May 2020 to January 2023 is 33 months.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2023 1 1) EQUALS 33
-- Payable April 2025 is exactly 60 months after April 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS 60
-- Payable May 2025 would be 61 months: capped at 60.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — A, the number of months from the month after the contributor reaches 65 years of age to the month the pension becomes payable, or 60` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS 60

§§ `78.4 -- B, by the month the pension becomes payable`

#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2010 12 31) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2011 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0057
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2011 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0057
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2012 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0064
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2012 12 31) EQUALS JUST 0.0064
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2013 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0070
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — B, the increase for each month` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS JUST 0.0070

§§ `78.4 -- the adjustment factor, 1 + (A x B)`

-- Born 15 March 1955, payable January 2023: A is 33, B is 0.0070, so 1 + 0.231 = 1.231.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2023 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.231
-- Capped: payable January 2026 is 69 months after April 2020, so A is 60: 1 + 0.42 = 1.42.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.42
-- Born 15 March 1945 reaches 65 in April 2010. Payable January 2011: A is 9, B is 0.0057, so 1 + 0.0513 = 1.0513.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1945 3 15) (YMD 2011 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.0513
-- Payable December 2011: A is 20, B is 0.0057, so 1 + 0.114 = 1.114.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1945 3 15) (YMD 2011 12 1) EQUALS JUST 1.114
-- Payable January 2012: A is 21, B is 0.0064, so 1 + 0.1344 = 1.1344.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1945 3 15) (YMD 2012 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.1344
-- Payable December 2012: A is 32, B is 0.0064, so 1 + 0.2048 = 1.2048.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1945 3 15) (YMD 2012 12 1) EQUALS JUST 1.2048
-- Payable January 2013: A is 33, B is 0.0070, so 1 + 0.231 = 1.231.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1945 3 15) (YMD 2013 1 1) EQUALS JUST 1.231
-- Payable before 2011 (but after reaching 65): no B in the text, so not covered. Born 1940, 65 in 2005, payable 2008.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1940 3 15) (YMD 2008 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Payable in or before the month of reaching 65: regulation 78.4 does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` (YMD 1955 3 15) (YMD 2019 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
